2. The country table

   data/countries.json is adapted from:

   United Nations, Department of Economic and Social Affairs, Population Division
   (2024). World Population Prospects 2024, Online Edition. Demographic Indicators,
   medium variant (WPP2024_Demographic_Indicators_Medium.csv.gz).
   https://population.un.org/wpp/

   The source data are licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 3.0 IGO
   License (CC BY 3.0 IGO): https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/igo/

   Changes made to the source data:
   - only countries and areas with an ISO2 code are kept;
   - only life expectancy at birth (LEx, LExMale, LExFemale) for 2023 is kept;
   - the values are rounded to two decimal places;
   - the location names are replaced with the short English names in
     data/country-names.json.

   The adapted table is available under CC BY 4.0 with the attribution above to
   the United Nations kept. The United Nations does not endorse this package or
   the way the data are used in it.
